That run confirmed the remaining issue is proof structure, not program behavior: a top-level call claim alone keeps unrolling arbitrary-length loops. I’m adding the standard circular loop invariant at the function-frame boundary, with an accumulator-shaped specification so one symbolic iteration returns to exactly the same claim shape.
apply patch
